  "title": "Operation of the Portuguese Contingency Heatwaves Plan",
  "summary": "Successful implementation of a national heatwave contingency plan requires monitoring of the state of health and socio-economic conditions of individuals, the health system, the specific location, and the frequency with which extreme temperatures occur in that location. The Portuguese Heatwave Contingency Plan was developed to implement corrective measure to be taken when required, i.e. to prevent the adverse health impacts from elevated temperatures, also considering the possible impacts of climate change. Evidence that elevated temperatures can lead to increased mortality and morbidity is well documented, with population vulnerability being location specific.",
